  "chapter": 691,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 70 Chapter 691\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4585, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the public health law and the insurance law, in\n        relation to  promoting  efficient  and  effective  oversight  of\n        continuing  care  retirement  communities; and to repeal certain\n        provisions of such law relating thereto\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill seeks to achieve three goals: first, to change the  role  of\nthe  Continuing  Care Retirement Community (CCRC) Council to advisory by\ndelegating its duties to the Department  of  Health  (DOH);  second,  to\npermit  the  Commissioner  of  Health  to  increase priority reservation\namounts; and third, to move the tasks related to financial oversight  of\nCCRCs from the Department of Financial Services (DFS) to DOH.\n \n  I support the first two goals of this legislation. The CCRC Council is\ncurrently  tasked  with  approving applications to become a CCRC, but an\ninability to meet quorum requirements can cause  unnecessary  delays  in\nthe  process.  Changing it to an advisory council will retain the exper-\ntise of the CCRC Council  and  streamline  the  CCRC  approval  process.\nFurthermore,   permitting  the  Commissioner  of  Health  to  use  their\ndiscretion to increase the permissible amounts associated with  priority\nreservations will reduce the administrative burdens on CCRCs. However, I\ndo  not  agree  that CCRCs would be better regulated by moving financial\noversight from DFS to DOH.  The specialized knowledge and infrastructure\nnecessary for this work is primarily used in  the  insurance  industries\nand is appropriately housed within DFS.\n \n  I  have  reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact changes in\nthe upcoming legislative session to improve the processes around licens-\ning and regulations of CCRCs. On the  basis  of  this  agreement,  I  am\npleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
